Convex 1.44.0. `items` has `{ name: string, expiresAt: number }` and an index `by_expiresAt` on `["expiresAt"]`. All times are Unix milliseconds.

```ts
import { query } from "./_generated/server";
import { v } from "convex/values";
export const listActive = query({
  args: { now: v.number() },
  handler: async (ctx, args) => {
    return await ctx.db.query("items")
      .withIndex("by_expiresAt", q => q.gt("expiresAt", args.now))
      .take(100);
  },
});
```

The only item expires at `T + 1000`. A client subscribes with `{ now: T }` and receives that item. No documents change. The client clock passes `T + 2000`, while the subscription arguments stay unchanged. The client then replaces the subscription with one using `{ now: T + 2000 }`.
